WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:06.833
Bonnie?

2
00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:11.833
Aren't you ever gonna get out of bed?

3
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.266
- Please wake up.
- Huh?

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.500
Clemont, why are you dressed like that?

5
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.966
What do you mean? It's my wedding day, remember?

6
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:24.933
- Huh? Wedding?
- Right.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.400
I'm also going to turn the Lumiose Gym over to you. Take good care of it.

8
00:00:31.266 --> 00:00:32.966
Wait, you can't do that.

9
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.400
Come on. Get dressed or we'll be late.

10
00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:37.533
Wear something nice on my big day.

11
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:52.033
Wait!

12
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.900
Come on, you can't really be getting married.

13
00:00:54.966 --> 00:00:56.066
Stop it now!

14
00:00:58.366 --> 00:01:01.133
Clemont, stop it!

15
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:08.400
Whew. No way. That wouldn't have happened.

16
00:01:08.466 --> 00:01:10.933
It couldn't. Impossible.

17
00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:18.900
Yay. Yippee.

18
00:01:23.966 --> 00:01:27.266
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

19
00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:31.200
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

20
00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:35.100
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

21
00:01:35.166 --> 00:01:37.766
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

22
00:01:38.366 --> 00:01:39.433
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

23
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.666
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

24
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:45.900
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

25
00:01:45.966 --> 00:01:47.633
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

26
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.333
Our heroes are continuing their journey to Snowbelle City,

27
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.400
where Ash hopes to win his eighth Kalos Gym badge.

28
00:02:05.466 --> 00:02:06.833
A strange dream?

29
00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.733
- Yeah. It was so weird.
- What do you mean?

30
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.400
Hmm? Can't tell, 'cause it's a secret.

31
00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.433
Dreams can come true, right?

32
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.333
- So, dream carefully.
- Carefully?

33
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.866
It's like "Be careful what you wish for, 'cause you might get it."

34
00:02:22.866 --> 00:02:25.700
Hey, Clemont. Aren't you gonna eat your breakfast?

35
00:02:25.766 --> 00:02:27.200
Pika, Pika.

36
00:02:27.266 --> 00:02:29.166
I'll be there in just a minute.

37
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.633
Oh, well. Guess I blew it again.

38
00:02:37.266 --> 00:02:39.966
- Me worried? No way.
- Huh?

39
00:02:57.633 --> 00:02:59.766
Buneary. Buneary.

40
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:01.166
Huh?

41
00:03:02.633 --> 00:03:03.666
Bun, Bun.

42
00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:13.066
- Bunnelby.
- Bun?

43
00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.266
- You find it?
- Bunnelby.

44
00:03:15.333 --> 00:03:18.366
- Huh?
- Look at that. See?

45
00:03:18.433 --> 00:03:19.733
It's a Buneary.

46
00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:25.100
Buneary. The Rabbit Pokémon.

47
00:03:25.166 --> 00:03:29.766
Perks up its ears at the first sign of danger. It tucks its head into its fur

48
00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:32.733
- to sleep on cold nights.
- It's adorable.

49
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.100
Sure is.

50
00:03:34.166 --> 00:03:36.500
Buneary, where are you?

51
00:03:37.266 --> 00:03:40.633
- Buneary.
- That's where you are.

52
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.466
My, my. Are they friends?

53
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:47.300
- Excuse me. Is that Buneary with you?
- That's right.

54
00:03:47.366 --> 00:03:49.466
I'll bet that Bunnelby's with you.

55
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.166
- You're right.
- What a pretty girl.

56
00:03:52.233 --> 00:03:56.500
You're a keeper! Help me out. Please take care of my brother.

57
00:03:57.566 --> 00:03:58.433
Uh...

58
00:03:58.866 --> 00:04:03.933
You could be my big brother's wife. He's reliable, but he makes things

59
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.200
that sometimes don't work. He needs someone to keep him grounded.

60
00:04:07.266 --> 00:04:10.466
Stop. I told you not to do that a million times.

61
00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.533
Stop it! No fair!

62
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.133
That sounds interesting. Actually, I'm looking for a partner, too.

63
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.899
I'm Lilia. Hi there.

64
00:04:19.966 --> 00:04:21.500
Huh?

65
00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:25.066
- Hey, what's that?
- It's my Aipom Arm.

66
00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.400
That's really cool.

67
00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.833
I made it myself.

68
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.066
Incredible.

69
00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.700
I'm really interested in devices like this.

70
00:04:33.633 --> 00:04:35.466
- Please.
- Thank you.

71
00:04:36.166 --> 00:04:39.966
Wow. So, your father's the president of Orangics?

72
00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.333
- Incredible.
- He sure is.

73
00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.733
I can't believe it.

74
00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.400
Orangics is the world's number one manufacturer of robots.

75
00:04:47.466 --> 00:04:48.300
Awesome.

76
00:04:48.366 --> 00:04:51.033
- Wow, talk about cool.
- Pikachu.

77
00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.433
Beyond amazing.

78
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.333
It's true.

79
00:04:53.766 --> 00:04:57.766
Even so, your Aipom Arm is more amazing. By a mile.

80
00:04:57.833 --> 00:05:01.266
Clemont's great at coming up with all sorts of machines.

81
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:02.566
I don't know.

82
00:05:02.633 --> 00:05:05.333
The thing is, it's really just a hobby.

83
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.900
He also made a robot named Clembot.

84
00:05:07.966 --> 00:05:09.066
Huh?

85
00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:10.266
Blabbermouth.

86
00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.866
They're all so fascinating.

87
00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:21.533
I keep the Aipom Arm hidden in my backpack and ready to go.

88
00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:25.000
What a great idea. Then you can use it anytime.

89
00:05:25.433 --> 00:05:26.966
Clemont's such a big help.

90
00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.600
He's gotten us out of a whole lot of really tough spots.

91
00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:31.633
- Mm-hm.
- Wow.

92
00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:35.266
So, Lilia, didn't you say you were looking for a partner?

93
00:05:35.333 --> 00:05:39.233
Yes, I did. I'll have to take over for my father someday.

94
00:05:39.666 --> 00:05:41.866
You're going to become president?

95
00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.800
Likely. But the partner I end up choosing will have to be ready, too.

96
00:05:46.866 --> 00:05:48.133
Makes sense to me.

97
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.033
That's great.

98
00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.000
It can't be.

99
00:05:51.966 --> 00:05:53.333
Clemont!

100
00:05:54.733 --> 00:05:56.266
- Wait, no.
- Bonnie?

101
00:05:56.733 --> 00:05:59.466
I'm sorry. I haven't introduced you two yet.

102
00:06:00.633 --> 00:06:04.766
- I want you to meet my bride, Lilia.
- Hi there. Nice to meet you.

103
00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.633
Now that we run Orangics, you're gonna help me out a bit.

104
00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.733
I'm going to put you in charge of the Lumiose Gym.

105
00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:18.566
Darling, your tea is all ready.

106
00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:21.200
- Why don't you take a break?
- Thank you, dear.

107
00:06:25.766 --> 00:06:28.833
- No. No way.
- Dedenne!

108
00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:33.633
- Hey, what's the matter, Bonnie?
- Do me a favor. Pinch my cheek hard.

109
00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.800
- What for?
- Do it, please.

110
00:06:35.866 --> 00:06:37.000
Uh...

111
00:06:37.066 --> 00:06:38.800
Owie!

112
00:06:38.866 --> 00:06:39.833
That hurts.

113
00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.433
I'm awake. So, it isn't a dream.

114
00:06:44.066 --> 00:06:45.433
Oh.

115
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.500
- Are you hungry?
- Maybe I should make lunch.

116
00:06:48.933 --> 00:06:51.600
Clemont's a really great cook. He's amazing.

117
00:06:51.666 --> 00:06:53.866
Well, that would be wonderful.

118
00:06:53.933 --> 00:06:55.533
Double blabbermouth.

119
00:07:00.766 --> 00:07:03.933
Wow, a machine that can cook? I'm impressed.

120
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.466
Excuse me. I'm hungry, too, you know.

121
00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.866
You just had something to eat a little while ago.

122
00:07:09.933 --> 00:07:12.400
- Whatever.
- Dedenne.

123
00:07:12.466 --> 00:07:13.300
Hey, look.

124
00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.900
Buneary seems to like Bunnelby.

125
00:07:32.533 --> 00:07:34.333
Pancham.

126
00:07:42.633 --> 00:07:44.433
Dig it. It's a Buneary.

127
00:07:45.233 --> 00:07:48.933
- The epitome of cute.
- With Buneary in my hot little hands,

128
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.033
the whole wide world would be at my command.

129
00:07:52.166 --> 00:07:55.833
My ravishing beauty would be lifted up to a whole new level.

130
00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.733
You don't say.

131
00:07:58.166 --> 00:07:59.533
I do say.

132
00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.233
That's the way this old world goes round.

133
00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:03.233
I'm dizzy.

134
00:08:03.666 --> 00:08:08.166
One can never be too beautiful. So, we're catching that Buneary, see?

135
00:08:08.233 --> 00:08:09.233
Crystal clear.

136
00:08:09.666 --> 00:08:12.333
You know, that Buneary might just be the thing

137
00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.500
to warm Team Rocket right up.

138
00:08:14.933 --> 00:08:18.000
- Like a hot plate?
- Let me give it to you straight.

139
00:08:18.066 --> 00:08:21.833
Whether it's Inkay or Gourgeist... they're not all that cute.

140
00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:23.900
I think Inkay's adorable.

141
00:08:24.333 --> 00:08:26.266
Not much warmth going on there.

142
00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.266
It's decided. We catch Buneary.

143
00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:31.700
Mm.

144
00:08:31.766 --> 00:08:33.733
Delicious. Such great food.

145
00:08:33.799 --> 00:08:34.866
Told you so.

146
00:08:34.933 --> 00:08:37.066
A man who can cook. Lovely.

147
00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:38.766
Stop. I'm blushing.

148
00:08:38.833 --> 00:08:40.633
- Huh?
- Dedenne.

149
00:08:41.933 --> 00:08:43.566
Here. Try this.

150
00:08:43.633 --> 00:08:46.066
A little sweet honey for a sweetheart.

151
00:08:47.333 --> 00:08:48.600
Like you.

152
00:08:51.066 --> 00:08:53.566
Wow. That's so sweet.

153
00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.500
Ah.

154
00:08:55.566 --> 00:08:57.466
All right. Say "ah."

155
00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.833
Ah. Mm, mm, mm.

156
00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.233
Delicious.

157
00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.100
And then Clemont will say:

158
00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:08.266
I'm the happiest man in the whole world.

159
00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.133
What was that for? You know you shouldn't do that.

160
00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.333
- Now apologize.
- Denne.

161
00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.500
No. It's okay

162
00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:32.000
- Nice job. Thanks, Dedenne.
- Dedenne.

163
00:09:34.266 --> 00:09:36.666
- You two.
- Huh?

164
00:09:36.733 --> 00:09:38.866
Why don't you go for a little walk?

165
00:09:38.933 --> 00:09:42.166
- Buneary.
- Bunnelby.

166
00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:47.000
Bunnelby, take care of Buneary.

167
00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:53.800
Bunnelby's extremely reliable. You don't have to worry about a thing.

168
00:09:53.866 --> 00:09:56.533
Mm-hm. Say, why don't we go, too?

169
00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.566
Come on. Let's take a walk.

170
00:09:58.633 --> 00:10:00.033
Sure. Sounds fun.

171
00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:03.166
Just because Buneary and Bunnelby get along so well

172
00:10:03.233 --> 00:10:05.933
doesn't mean they have to take a walk together, too.

173
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.033
Dedenne.

174
00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.833
- That's so sweet, isn't it?
- Huh?

175
00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.600
I have a feeling things might work out for those two.

176
00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.900
I wish I had never said she's a keeper.

177
00:10:18.966 --> 00:10:22.566
That's right. Once I was even kicked out of my own gym.

178
00:10:30.833 --> 00:10:33.666
- Lilia! Are you okay?
- Buneary.

179
00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.400
I think so.

180
00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.433
We missed.

181
00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.266
We got the girl with the glasses. Not Buneary.

182
00:10:40.333 --> 00:10:41.500
Lousy aim.

183
00:10:41.566 --> 00:10:42.766
On to plan B.

184
00:10:44.233 --> 00:10:45.400
Grab hold.

185
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.666
Thanks so much.

186
00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:51.500
- Buneary.
- Bunnelby.

187
00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:54.800
- There you go.
- Thanks.

188
00:10:55.233 --> 00:10:57.033
You're so sweet and kind.

189
00:10:57.133 --> 00:10:59.633
Oh, it really wasn't anything.

190
00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:02.733
- Lilia?
- Huh?

191
00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.666
Can I talk to you for a minute?

192
00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:06.933
Sure.

193
00:11:07.466 --> 00:11:08.366
Over here.

194
00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:15.300
- Hmm. What are they doing?
- Bonnie's a good little sister.

195
00:11:15.366 --> 00:11:17.266
Huh? Yeah.

196
00:11:18.933 --> 00:11:22.500
Wow. So, your brother makes all sorts of inventions, doesn't he?

197
00:11:22.566 --> 00:11:26.233
- Seems like they're all really incredible.
- They all blow up.

198
00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:29.266
Every single one of them. They're all disasters.

199
00:11:29.333 --> 00:11:31.800
- Dedenne.
- They go boom, and it makes a mess.

200
00:11:31.866 --> 00:11:32.833
De, ne, ne

201
00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.066
Failure leads to success.

202
00:11:35.133 --> 00:11:38.433
That's how truly great inventions get perfected.

203
00:11:39.966 --> 00:11:42.433
Know what? He gets scared of the dark.

204
00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.533
- Like a baby.
- Dedenne.

205
00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.833
How sweet. That's so adorable.

206
00:11:47.766 --> 00:11:51.200
Also, know what else? He likes to take off his shirt...

207
00:11:51.266 --> 00:11:55.833
and wrap himself in an Arbok, like a blankie.

208
00:11:56.266 --> 00:11:57.466
That's so nice.

209
00:11:57.533 --> 00:12:00.366
An Arbok can be so cozy and warm.

210
00:12:03.133 --> 00:12:05.900
That didn't go well.

211
00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:08.100
Who's that Pokémon?

212
00:12:13.333 --> 00:12:15.966
- It's Buneary.
- Buneary!

213
00:12:21.333 --> 00:12:23.866
- Okay, let's hit it.
- Pika.

214
00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:27.366
Mind if I walk to the next Pokémon Center with you?

215
00:12:27.433 --> 00:12:28.833
Sure. Let's all go.

216
00:12:29.266 --> 00:12:31.933
- Yeah, come on.
- Dedenne.

217
00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.833
So... is your leg all right?

218
00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.266
Yes, it's fine now. Doesn't hurt a bit.

219
00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.666
Clemont. Let's hold hands.

220
00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.566
- But, Bonnie, you never wanna hold hands.
- Come on.

221
00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:51.633
What happened?

222
00:12:54.033 --> 00:12:55.833
- What happened?
- What was that?

223
00:12:56.933 --> 00:12:58.966
- Buneary.
- Bunnel.

224
00:13:01.866 --> 00:13:03.266
- Now what?
- Pika!

225
00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.100
Prepare for trouble. All's fair in love.

226
00:13:07.166 --> 00:13:09.866
And make it double. It fits like a glove.

227
00:13:09.933 --> 00:13:14.766
- To protect the world from devastation.
- To unite all couples within our nation.

228
00:13:14.833 --> 00:13:17.533
To denounce the evils of hearts and flowers.

229
00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.366
To extend our reach into the wee, small hours.

230
00:13:21.266 --> 00:13:22.933
- Jessie.
- And James.

231
00:13:23.566 --> 00:13:26.466
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

232
00:13:26.533 --> 00:13:29.500
Surrender now or prepare for a heartfelt fight.

233
00:13:29.566 --> 00:13:31.300
Meowth, that's right.

234
00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.966
Pit trap courtesy of us.

235
00:13:35.033 --> 00:13:36.266
It's you guys.

236
00:13:36.333 --> 00:13:38.366
Give back Buneary and Bunnelby.

237
00:13:38.733 --> 00:13:39.566
Who are they?

238
00:13:39.633 --> 00:13:42.233
Bad guys who steal other people's Pokémon.

239
00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.033
Pika.

240
00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.033
We've just grabbed these cutie-pie Pokémon for a song.

241
00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.566
So long.

242
00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.800
You two. Are you both okay?

243
00:14:01.133 --> 00:14:03.566
Clemont, get us out of here.

244
00:14:03.966 --> 00:14:04.800
Lilia.

245
00:14:07.533 --> 00:14:08.933
I need to get out, too!

246
00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:10.600
Poor Buneary.

247
00:14:10.666 --> 00:14:13.966
I promise you, I'll get Buneary and Bunnelby back here,

248
00:14:14.033 --> 00:14:15.500
- safe and sound.
- Thanks.

249
00:14:15.966 --> 00:14:19.333
See, the future is now, thanks to science.

250
00:14:19.833 --> 00:14:21.533
Clemontic Gear, on.

251
00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:25.033
I thought we'd encounter a situation precisely like this.

252
00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:27.900
My Protection Progress Machine.

253
00:14:28.533 --> 00:14:32.933
There are transmitters embedded in the bandages I put on you and Buneary.

254
00:14:34.533 --> 00:14:35.700
See what it does?

255
00:14:37.433 --> 00:14:38.700
It's responding.

256
00:14:39.166 --> 00:14:41.100
Wow, science is so amazing.

257
00:14:41.333 --> 00:14:42.733
So, let's begin.

258
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.200
I've got a signal.

259
00:14:48.866 --> 00:14:51.933
- All right. Let's find them.
- Let's go.

260
00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:03.033
Our own sweetie.

261
00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.733
It's a cutie crew.

262
00:15:06.066 --> 00:15:08.500
- Buneary! Bunnelby!
- Huh?

263
00:15:08.566 --> 00:15:11.533
- How did you find us?
- My brother's invention.

264
00:15:11.966 --> 00:15:13.900
Gourgeist, make them pay.

265
00:15:13.966 --> 00:15:15.666
Yay, Inkay.

266
00:15:16.166 --> 00:15:17.400
- Gourg!
- Inkay!

267
00:15:17.466 --> 00:15:18.666
Use shadow ball.

268
00:15:21.433 --> 00:15:23.400
Chespin, now. Pin missile.

269
00:15:23.466 --> 00:15:24.966
Chespin!

270
00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.233
- All right, Pikachu, thunderbolt.
- Pika!

271
00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.300
Pikachu!

272
00:15:31.366 --> 00:15:32.700
Quick. Psybeam.

273
00:15:35.266 --> 00:15:36.533
Luxray, help us out.

274
00:15:38.466 --> 00:15:40.600
- Ray.
- Use thunder fang.

275
00:15:45.466 --> 00:15:47.000
Use psybeam once more.

276
00:15:47.066 --> 00:15:48.366
And shadow ball.

277
00:15:55.333 --> 00:15:56.200
Bonnie, no!

278
00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:01.166
Bonnie!

279
00:16:04.033 --> 00:16:06.433
- Clemont!
- You're going to be fine.

280
00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.333
Mm-hm.

281
00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.400
Use shadow ball.

282
00:16:10.166 --> 00:16:11.366
Dodge it, quick.

283
00:16:12.333 --> 00:16:14.266
Now, Pancham, it's our turn.

284
00:16:14.333 --> 00:16:15.600
Use stone edge.

285
00:16:15.666 --> 00:16:17.633
Pancham!

286
00:16:19.533 --> 00:16:21.500
- Seed bomb, go.
- Gourgeist, geist, geist!

287
00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:25.300
Bonnie, just stay still!

288
00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.800
- I'm pulling you up right now.
- Can you do it?

289
00:16:28.866 --> 00:16:30.400
- Luxray?
- Of course I can.

290
00:16:35.366 --> 00:16:37.300
- Clemont!
- It's okay!

291
00:16:37.366 --> 00:16:39.600
Trust me. And my Aipom Arm, too.

292
00:16:41.133 --> 00:16:42.166
Hmm.

293
00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.366
See? Everything's all right.

294
00:16:58.733 --> 00:17:00.766
- You did it.
- What a relief.

295
00:17:00.833 --> 00:17:02.066
- Ray.
- Oh!

296
00:17:03.333 --> 00:17:04.800
Braixen, it's your turn.

297
00:17:05.233 --> 00:17:07.133
- Fire blast.
- Braixen.

298
00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:10.033
Braixen!

299
00:17:11.366 --> 00:17:12.700
Pikachu, electro ball.

300
00:17:12.766 --> 00:17:15.166
Pikachu!

301
00:17:17.066 --> 00:17:19.900
- Are you all right?
- Yeah, I'm just fine.

302
00:17:20.433 --> 00:17:22.599
But your Aipom Arm isn't.

303
00:17:23.099 --> 00:17:25.233
Oh, I can fix this thing easily.

304
00:17:26.433 --> 00:17:30.100
The important thing is it saved you. And that's what matters.

305
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.266
Oh, Clemont.

306
00:17:42.966 --> 00:17:45.500
These warm-and-cuddlies are staying right here.

307
00:17:45.566 --> 00:17:47.033
- Buneary.
- Bunnelby.

308
00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.300
Pikachu, use iron tail to cut through that net.

309
00:17:50.366 --> 00:17:51.533
Pikachu.

310
00:17:57.733 --> 00:17:59.833
- Yes.
- Thank goodness you're safe.

311
00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:01.600
- Bunnelby.
- Boneary.

312
00:18:01.666 --> 00:18:02.733
Yeah.

313
00:18:03.666 --> 00:18:04.900
Guess what's next.

314
00:18:04.966 --> 00:18:06.466
Pikachu, thunderbolt.

315
00:18:06.533 --> 00:18:09.200
Pika! Pikachu!

316
00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:17.900
Buneary would've lifted my ravishing beauty up a notch,

317
00:18:17.966 --> 00:18:20.866
raising my allure up from a ten to an 11.

318
00:18:21.466 --> 00:18:24.600
No doubt Team Rocket would've had more cuddle power.

319
00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.966
- But Inkay's still my cutie of the hour.
- Inkay.

320
00:18:28.033 --> 00:18:30.566
We're blasting off again!

321
00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.900
- Oh, Buneary. Is everything all right?
- Bun.

322
00:18:36.966 --> 00:18:38.966
I'm just glad everybody's safe.

323
00:18:39.033 --> 00:18:40.900
Thanks so much, Clemont.

324
00:18:40.966 --> 00:18:43.200
- All of you.
- It was nothing.

325
00:18:45.733 --> 00:18:46.766
Mm.

326
00:18:47.366 --> 00:18:50.633
- Well, then... time to say goodbye.
- Huh?

327
00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:54.066
I thought you were coming with us to the Pokémon Center.

328
00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:57.766
Not now. I'm not ready to choose a partner just yet.

329
00:18:57.833 --> 00:19:01.233
There's still a lot more for me to learn. An awful lot.

330
00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:04.900
It's not the kind of quick decision you make overnight.

331
00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:08.366
- Pika?
- Mm?

332
00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.433
Bonnie, be nice to your brother, okay?

333
00:19:16.233 --> 00:19:17.066
Okay.

334
00:19:18.933 --> 00:19:20.266
Let's go, Buneary.

335
00:19:26.266 --> 00:19:29.866
- Take care of yourself, Lilia.
- Pika, Pika!

336
00:19:29.933 --> 00:19:31.433
We'll see you again.

337
00:19:31.866 --> 00:19:34.433
Lilia, bye!

338
00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.800
- Buneary!
- Bunnelby!

339
00:19:36.866 --> 00:19:38.233
Have a good time!

340
00:19:39.466 --> 00:19:42.600
You're fine the way you are, Clemont. You know?

341
00:19:42.666 --> 00:19:45.200
Huh? What are you talking about?

342
00:19:45.266 --> 00:19:46.633
Dedenne.

343
00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:47.633
Nothing.

344
00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:53.700
After being rescued by her big brother,

345
00:19:53.766 --> 00:19:56.566
Bonnie was reminded of just how close they are.

346
00:19:56.933 --> 00:19:59.766
Now it's off once again to Snowbelle City,

347
00:19:59.833 --> 00:20:03.800
and Ash's next gym battle, as the journey continues.

348
00:20:08.366 --> 00:20:10.933
Okay. Let's see how this works.

349
00:20:11.366 --> 00:20:13.666
- Is it fixed?
- Good as new.

350
00:20:14.233 --> 00:20:16.900
Huh? Hmm.

351
00:20:16.966 --> 00:20:18.700
Uh... what about this?

352
00:20:30.133 --> 00:20:31.466
Guess I was right.

353
00:20:31.633 --> 00:20:34.566
I really do need to find someone to take care of you.

354
00:20:34.633 --> 00:20:35.566
Huh?

355
00:20:35.633 --> 00:20:36.766
Someone like you.

356
00:20:36.833 --> 00:20:39.766
You're a keeper. Please take care of my brother.

357
00:20:39.933 --> 00:20:41.933
- Who? Me?
- Bonnie!

358
00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:46.200
I told you not to do this a million times!
